// Ch15 B09 "The current-song" (C, 2 min) and B10 "The dock-master" (C, 2 min). act2_ch15.md §2 B09-B10.
// H01: 05:40, thick grey fog, no horizon. Liss stands up from the bier for the first time since the court.
// H02: she sings a Saltwright current-song (a sung chart of the sea's currents; ADR 0204 §10: Liss sings it
// in `hollowmere_answers`), unaccompanied, rough from the night. It is Hollowmere's, NEVER Dace's
// `current_song`. Rhen turns at the first phrase: the same FAMILY of song as the one in the storm. He says
// nothing (a seed for Ch17). H03: silence; then an answer from the south, many voices singing the chart's
// next phrase, and lashed hulls coming out of the white. Liss keeps singing until a line can be thrown.
// B10 is ch15_the_dock_master.dlg (split 2026-10-30: B10 is staged in ch17/hollowmere; this file is the open sea).
// B10 (H04-H06): Hollowmere at dawn, the first oil lamps on the hulls (rule 3 ends). Aldous Varrow, the
// dock-master, at his hull-house door; he looks at the canopy, then at his daughter. H06: from the barge,
// at a distance, Liss tells him. NO DIALOGUE IS HEARD in this beat: the errand is hers.
title: ch15_current_song
location: ch15/open_sea
---
@letterbox on
@fade in 3.0
@camera H01
@mark liss bow_liss walk
@wait 3.0
@camera H02
@music hollowmere_answers fade=0.0
@anim liss sing
@wait 3.0
@anim rhen look_at liss
@wait 4.0
@camera H03
@wait 8.0
<<set $ch15_hollowmere_answered = true>>
@fade out 1.5
@letterbox off
===
